{
 "purpose": "Batch-2 paint specs for the existing procedural shoe shell. Same coordinates/evaluation as shoe_paint_spec.json (batch 1, unchanged), plus 3 additions.",
 "inherits": "shoe_paint_spec.json (coordinates, window, evaluation, tiers)",
 "additions": {
  "ellipse": "layer key ellipse={c:[v,sx], r:[rv,rsx], e:soft}: weight *= 1-smoothstep(1-e,1,d), d=sqrt(((v-cv)/rv)^2+((sx-csx)/rsx)^2); still multiplied by the u/v/sx windows (use u to limit it to the toe top / side).",
  "$body": "layer colour '$body' = the Jelly's own body colour at runtime (the foot shows through; ballet flats opening).",
  "glow": "layer flag glow:true = Swift drives emission on that layer's weight (additive bloom, pulse/colour-cycle cyan<->pink while walking/running); the baked colour is the idle look."
 },
 "visible_note": "At game camera the body hides u>~0.6 over most of the foot: identity must live on the toe cap, sides, sole and midsole (which these specs do). The shell resolution limits detail to ~0.05 in u/v.",
